      "description": "Instructor, Pre-Licensure Nursing (Gilbert) (On-Call/Per Diem) (Multiple Positions) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor, Pre-Licensure Nursing (Gilbert) (On-Call/Per Diem) (Multiple Positions) Gilbert, AZ, United States | req27284 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Instructor, Pre-Licensure Nursing (Gilbert) (On-Call/Per Diem) (Multiple Positions) Posting Number req27284 Department College of Nursing Department Website Link https://nursing.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Greater Phoenix Area Address 92 W. Vaughn Ave #301, Gilbert, AZ 85233 USA Position Highlights Join one of our nationally ranked, CCNE-accredited pre-licensure nursing programs as a per diem Instructor and help shape the future of nursing education. We're seeking passionate nurses for our BSN-Integrative Health and MS-Entry to the Profession of Nursing programs. In this student-facing role based in Maricopa County, you'll guide students through skills labs, simulations, and clinical practice, helping them succeed in their degrees, pass the NCLEX, and launch successful careers as RNs. Our collaborative, innovative environment is nationally accredited and highly ranked. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Teach and guide students in\n       clinical and practical courses related to assigned programs. Provide instruction   for students during skills labs, simulations, and/or clinicals, which may   include assigned day shifts, night shift, or weekend experiences. Occupational health and\n       safety: Must satisfy clinical site compliance requirements (complete\n       drug screening, BLS, vaccination requirements, and/or additional\n       background check). Minimum Qualifications Applicants with a Bachelor’s degree: Bachelor’s degree in nursing (BSN) AND at least three years of clinical experience as an RN providing direct patient care. Enrollment in or completion of applicable graduate-level coursework OR possession of relevant national certification. Applicants with a Graduate degree: Graduate Degree in Nursing, or a related field, with at least two years of clinical experience as an RN providing direct patient care. Preferred Qualifications Graduate degree in nursing. Experience teaching in higher education. National certification in the area of clinical practice. Rank Instructor Tenure Information Part-Time Hourly (NTE) FLSA Non-Exempt Full Time/Part Time Part Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 0 - 19.5 Job FTE 0.025 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible No Benefits Rate of Pay Dayshift: $40-$50 per hour Nightshift: $50-$60 per hour Compensation Type hourly rate Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 10 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Lauren Acosta | heller@arizona.edu Open Date 10/7/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Three Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Must be able to provide evidence/receipt of an active Arizona RN License prior to first day of employment with College of Nursing. Must be eligible to obtain a Level 1 Fingerprint Clearance Card from AZDPS. Document Needed to apply Curriculum Vitae (CV) or Résumé Cover Letter Unofficial Academic Transcripts Proof of Current RN Licensure Names and Phone Numbers of at Least Three (3) Professional References Please submit all requested documents and complete the application in its entirety: In your Cover Letter , please address your teaching interest and experience; AND include the clinical areas listed below in which you have experience: Adult Medical-Surgical Case Management/Care Transitions Community/Community-based Population Health Critical Care Emergency/Trauma Health Promotion Hospice/Palliative Care Long Term Care Maternal Newborn Operating Room/Post Anesthesia Care Pediatric, Primary Care/Ambulatory Care Psychiatric/Behavioral Health Other applicable area Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
