    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27219?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Social & Personality Psychology (T/TE)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Social & Personality Psychology (T/TE) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, Social & Personality Psychology (T/TE) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27219 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, Social & Personality Psychology (T/TE) Posting Number req27219 Department Psychology Department Website Link https://psychology.arizona.edu Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The Department of Psychology at the University of Arizona seeks to hire a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Social/Personality Psychology. We are seeking applicants who will expand departmental empirical and/or methodological perspectives. We will consider all candidates with a productive research program in any area of social/personality psychology. Preferred, but not required, areas of expertise include data science (e.g., cutting-edge data collection and statistical methods) and/or health applications, for example pertaining to the UA Research Initiative on AI and healthcare . The faculty member will teach courses at the graduate and undergraduate levels and contribute to mentoring students from various backgrounds. In line with the University of Arizona’s Core Values , the ideal candidate will contribute to the teaching and mentorship of our growing and dynamic student body. We are also seeking applicants who are motivated to participate in outreach within Tucson’s rich community and contribute to departmental, college, and university service. The Department of Psychology has a robust record of interdisciplinary and collaborative research, with particular strengths in the areas of health psychology and health disparities, aging research, social affective neuroscience, methodological innovation, especially in the area of real-world assessment, prejudice reduction, cultural psychology, and the intersection between social, personality, and clinical psychology. We seek an exceptional scholar who will make connections across Psychology programs and with other departments as exemplified by the many interdisciplinary centers across the university. Applicants are expected to maintain an active research program with extramural funding. Respecting Identities and Supporting Empowerment are core values in the Psychology Department, and across the University of Arizona more broadly. At the University of Arizona, we know that different experiences and perspectives are vital to advancing innovation, critical thinking, and solving complex problems, and to creating a welcoming and collaborative academic community. Located in the beautiful desert Southwest, Tucson is nestled between the Catalina and Tucson Mountains and Saguaro National Park. This bicycle-friendly city is known for its arts, music, food, and rich history. Tucson is a designated UNESCO City of Gastronomy and is consistently ranked as one of the country’s best places to live . Formal review of applicants will begin November 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; sick leave and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Maintain an active research program with extramural funding. Teach\ncourses at the graduate and undergraduate levels and contribute to mentoring\nstudents. Contribute\nto departmental, college, and university service. Ideally, participate\nin outreach with Tucson’s rich community. Minimum Qualifications PhD\nin Psychology, or a closely related field by the start of the appointment. Record of potential for undergraduate- and graduate-level teaching and mentoring. Record of potential to maintain an active research program. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated potential to strengthen departmental empirical and/or methodological perspectives. Demonstrated potential to contribute to and add breadth to the Social/Personality Program. Demonstrated strengths in the areas of data science or health applications. Rank Assistant Professor Tenure Information Tenure Track (T/TE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Academic Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 8/16/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Requests for information or inquiries about the position can be sent to Search Chair, Dr. Daniel Sullivan at swolf22@arizona.edu. Open Date 10/6/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Four Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant The successful applicant is required to have a PhD in psychology, or a closely related field by the start of the appointment, as well as a record attesting to the potential for success in maintaining an active research program and teaching undergraduate- and graduate-level courses. Please attach the following materials to your application: A curriculum vitae (CV). A cover letter. Three reprints (combined into a single PDF for upload). A statement of research interests. A statement of teaching and mentoring experience. Contact information for three individuals who can provide letters of recommendation (letters may be solicited after the initial evaluation of applicants). The ideal applicant will use these materials to demonstrate ways in which their research, teaching, mentoring, and service can contribute to the University’s Core Values. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27158?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Immunology Assistant, Associate or Full Professor-Basic Medical Sciences (TT) (MD/PhD) (Phoenix)",
      "description": "Immunology Assistant, Associate or Full Professor-Basic Medical Sciences (TT) (MD/PhD) (Phoenix) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Immunology Assistant, Associate or Full Professor-Basic Medical Sciences (TT) (MD/PhD) (Phoenix) Phoenix, AZ, United States | req27158 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Immunology Assistant, Associate or Full Professor-Basic Medical Sciences (TT) (MD/PhD) (Phoenix) Posting Number req27158 Department COM Phx Basic Medical Sci Department Website Link College of Medicine-Phoenix Medical Sub-Speciality Location Greater Phoenix Area Address 475 N. 5th Street, Phoenix, AZ 85004 USA Position Highlights The Department of Basic Medical Sciences (BMS) at the University of Arizona College of Medicine – Phoenix seeks to hire assistant, associate or full professors in the broad area of immunology. The positions report directly to the department chair. The Department of Basic Medical Sciences at the College of Medicine – Phoenix is undergoing a significant and strategic expansion in the research enterprise. Growth of immunology is one of the strategic priorities of the college in the next period. To that effect, the department is seeking to recruit two new immunology tenured or tenure track faculty at the rank of assistant, associate or full professor in the broad area of immunology to complement and enhance the current cadre of highly innovative, collegial, collaborative and well-funded group of faculty within the department and college. Currently, the department's strengths include neuroscience, cancer, metabolic and cardiovascular diseases, and the new immunology faculty would be positioned to help the department move to the next level of collaborative science. These positions include overseeing and conducting an independent research program, conducting collaborative and programmatic research with other faculty, publishing findings in peer reviewed journals, pursuing and securing extramural funding and taking on duties and responsibilities that demonstrate strong service to the department and the college. This may include serving on committees, task forces, coordinating, overseeing or assisting in specific aspects of departmental operations. The successful candidates will fulfill the responsibilities of a faculty member within the Department of Basic Medical Sciences, actively participate in teaching, service and scholarly work, and must qualify for an appointment at the rank of assistant, associate or full professor. The successful candidates will meet the requirements of a tenure track faculty according to the College and University guidelines. Candidates with strong research programs in immunity to infection, inflammation and systems immunology are strongly encouraged to apply. Candidates with research programs not centrally related to immunology and inflammation will not be considered. The University of Arizona College of Medicine – Phoenix anchors the 28-acre Phoenix Biosciences Core (PBC) campus in the heart of the Valley of the Sun. The College inspires and trains individuals to become exemplary physicians, scientists and leaders who are life-long learners and inquisitive scholars. The PBC campus embodies the University’s priorities of engagement, partnership, innovation, and synergy in its world-class academic and research initiatives, with clinical facilities throughout Greater Phoenix. Visa sponsorship is available for this positions. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Develop innovative and collaborative immunology-related\n     research. Obtain extramural, including federal, support for research\n     programs and publish high impact scientific research in the broad areas of\n     immunology-related research. Develop collaborations with pertinent faculty within\n     the College and partner institutions; for senior candidates, lead larger programmatic\n     initiatives (P, U and similar grants) in their and related fields. Contribute to the teaching (medical, graduate and/or\n     other education), mentoring and service components of the College’s\n     missions. Other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Experience mentoring students and trainees in research projects. Outstanding interpersonal communication and professionalism skills. Minimum Qualifications Hold an MD, PhD or MD/PhD or an equivalent degree from an accredited institution in biological sciences, medicine or a related field. Exhibit a track record of high impact publications (all candidates), extramural research funding (preferrable for assistant professors, mandatory for other ranks) and teaching (associate and full professor level). Preferred Qualifications Demonstrate innovation and federally-funded (rank-appropriate) research in immunology and/or systems immunology. Have a strong track record in teaching and mentoring in classroom or laboratory settings (rank-appropriate). Have experience in an academic medical center and medical education environment. Exhibit a strong record of peer-reviewed publications in high-impact journals (rank-appropriate). Demonstrate experience with new techniques and approaches not currently available at the College of Medicine – Phoenix. Have experience serving on the editorial board of a peer-reviewed scientific journal (rank-appropriate). Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Tenure Track (T/TE) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay AAMC Public Schools for Rank and Specialty Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 2 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Office of Human Resources, Talent Acquisition talent@arizona.edu Open Date 10/6/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and Two Additional Documents Special Instructions to Applicant Application: The online application should be completed in its entirety. Blank or missed information may be considered an incomplete submission. CV, cover letter, and two additional documents are required to be considered for the position. One additional document will be a statement of research or teaching interest, which should clearly indicate your interest in this role and what skills or professional employment experience you have to support your application. The other additional document will be professional reference contacts. Please include at least three professional references at your current rank or above, their contact information, and the nature of your work with them. Faculty selected for this teaching opportunity will be required to obtain faculty status within the appropriate academic department. This will include obtaining letters of recommendation and review by the appropriate College review committee. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27231?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27231 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Posting Number req27231 Department Speech Language & Hearing Sci Department Website Link https://slhs.arizona.edu Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona’s Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences seeks a full-time Speech-Language Pathology Clinical Faculty member to serve as an SLP Placement Coordinator, with clinic management and clinical supervision duties as assigned. The successful candidate will participate in creating innovative SLP clinical education and service delivery opportunities at the University of Arizona. Experience in clinical education, student supervision, program development, project management, and culturally and linguistically sustaining clinical practice will help the candidate succeed in this role. The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences is renowned for its clinical training programs in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology, as well as its active doctoral program. Our department includes 30 faculty members, 104 graduate students in three-degree programs (M.S., Au.D, and Ph.D.), and 208 undergraduate students. Faculty in the department benefit from a rich collaborative environment within the University and the Southern Arizona communities. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Oversee and improve the M.S.\n     in SLP student placement and credentialing processes, both on campus and\n     off campus. Work with departmental leadership to maintain\n     active affiliation agreements with clinical sites. Direct the undergraduate and leveling student\n     observation and clinical experience programs. Cultivate and maintain robust relationships with\n     the regional and national speech-language pathologists who serve as\n     volunteer preceptors. Track student experiences and hours in compliance\n     with CAA and CFCC standards. Provide communication or feeding/swallowing\n     services at the on-site clinic or contracted site, depending on the area\n     of clinical specialization. Participate in the teaching, scholarship, and\n     service activities of our academic program. Perform additional administrative\n     responsibilities related to managing on-site or off-site clinics, as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications, corresponding to rank: Master’s\n     or doctoral degree in Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences, or\n     equivalent. Six years of experience\n     as a Speech-Language Pathologist with patient care responsibilities. License/license-eligibility\n     for practice in Speech-Language Pathology in the state of Arizona. Certificate of Clinical\n     Competence (CCC-SLP) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing\n     Association. Experience with\n     culturally and linguistically sustaining clinical practices. Preferred Qualifications Ten years of experience as a Speech-Language Pathologist with patient care responsibilities. Five years of experience in clinical education or supervision. Previous experience with successful program development. Prior experience with project management. Experience supporting skill development in SLPs and SLP students. Experience leading collaborative teams. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $75,000 - $120,000 (depending on rank) Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Robin Samlan, PhD, MBA, CCC-SLP Associate Professor, Associate Department Head & Director of Clinical Education rsamlan@arizona.edu Open Date 10/1/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Applicants should attach the following materials: Curriculum Vitae (CV). A cover letter that includes a description of your experience with, and approach to, clinical instruction. Contact information for three professional references. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27195?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice (General Practitioner - Surgery)(Oro Valley, AZ)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice (General Practitioner - Surgery)(Oro Valley, AZ) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice (General Practitioner - Surgery)(Oro Valley, AZ) Oro Valley, AZ, United States | req27195 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/29/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate Professor of Practice (General Practitioner - Surgery)(Oro Valley, AZ) Posting Number req27195 Department Vet Med Administration Department Website Link https://vetmed.arizona.edu/ Medical Sub-Speciality Location Outside of Tucson Address 1580 E. Hanley Blvd, Oro Valley, AZ 85737 USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona College of Veterinary Medicine (UA-CVM), located in Oro Valley, Arizona, invites applications for a faculty position with a primary focus on teaching veterinary surgery, anesthesia, and clinical management skills. We are seeking a veterinarian with clinical experience in small animal surgery to assist with the design and facilitation of active learning classroom sessions and labs for pre-clinical veterinary students. The UA-CVM curriculum is organized by organ-system blocks, and faculty in this position will collaborate with the organ-system course leaders to build clinically relevant surgical course content geared toward “day-one-ready” veterinarians. Course involvement will include supporting small animal surgery portions of medical and surgical courses, supporting the Clinical Skills courses and providing support in sessions for other system courses.  This position also has a research component that is focused on leading/ collaborating with other UA-CVM faculty on educational research. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Outstanding U of A benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; U of A/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to U of A recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Participate as a team member in the delivery of the pre-clinical small animal surgery simulation and live animal surgery hands on experiences. Oversee and assist students at various surgical sites to perform spays and neuters on local shelter animals as they perform different surgical roles within designated teams. Assist with the development and delivery of curriculum content to veterinary students within the UA-CVM vision of hands-on Immersive Simulation, Team-Based Learning and Peer Instruction pedagogy, in which students take substantial ownership of their learning, and didactic sessions are focused on the collaborative application of content. Participate as a team member in the design, development, and delivery of the pre-clinical small animal and/or equine/large animal clinical skills curriculum. Participate in the development and delivery of individual class sessions in other system courses and selectives. Provide reasonable out-of-classroom availability to various cohorts of veterinary students for office hours and scheduled meetings to assist students with learning. Engage in ongoing assessment and professional development aimed at the lifelong process of improving inclusive teaching and learning skills. Leading/collaborating with other UA-CVM faculty members on educational research. Engage in the CVM collegial community, the university community, and the larger global academic community through participation in shared governance, advisory committees, and academic/professional society meetings. Minimum Qualifications Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (DVM) degree (or international equivalent). At least two years of clinical experience performing small animal surgery. Preferred Qualifications At least four years of clinical experience performing small animal surgery. Prior experience in teaching and learning using active learning techniques, clinical skills instruction, and simulation-based education. Board certification or board eligibility in a relevant specialty such as small animal, equine, or large animal surgery. Prior experience in educational research. Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay DOE Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Frankie Kolb | fkolb@arizona.edu Open Date 9/29/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Additional Document: please submit a Brief (500-word limit) description of your philosophy on training and supporting students with hands-on clinical experiences, considering their wide range of backgrounds and skills, to ensure student success. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
    },
    "https://arizona.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/4/home/requisition/27086?c=arizona": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track)",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Tucson, AZ, United States | req27086 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/29/2026 Back to Search Assistant/Associate/Full Clinical Professor, Speech, Language, & Hearing Sciences (Career-Track) Posting Number req27086 Department Speech Language & Hearing Sci Department Website Link https://slhs.arizona.edu Medical Sub-Speciality Location Tucson Campus Address Tucson, AZ USA Position Highlights The University of Arizona’s Department of Speech Language, & Hearing Sciences seeks a Full-Time Speech-Language who will focus on service provision for children from Spanish-speaking or bilingual/multilingual communities.  The position may include travel and service provision in a regional community clinic where the majority of families speak Spanish The Department of Speech, Language, and Hearing Sciences is renowned for its clinical training programs in Audiology and Speech-Language Pathology, as well as its active doctoral program. Our department includes 30 faculty members, 104 graduate students in three degree programs (MS, AuD, PhD), and 208 undergraduate students. Faculty in the department benefit from rich collaborative environments within the university and the Southern Arizona communities. This career-track appointment is not eligible for tenure. Outstanding UA benefits include health, dental, and vision insurance plans; life insurance and disability programs; paid vacation, sick leave, and holidays; UA/ASU/NAU tuition reduction for the employee and qualified family members; retirement plans; access to UA recreation and cultural activities; and more! The University of Arizona has been recognized for our innovative work-life programs. For more information about working at the University of Arizona and relocations services, please click here . Duties & Responsibilities Provide evidence-based assessment and treatment to patients with communication and feeding disorders. Provide clinical services at the University clinic and a regional health center where the majority of the patients/families speak Spanish Supervise student clinicians Work with teaching faculty to reinforce concepts learned in the classroom Assist leadership with clinical administration and program development, as assigned Teach in the classroom related to area/s of expertise, as assigned Other duties, as assigned Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications, corresponding to rank: Master’s or doctoral degree Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences, or equivalent Three years of clinical experience as a Speech-Language Pathologist working with pediatric patients License/license-eligibility for practice in Speech-Language Pathology in the state of Arizona Certificate of Clinical Competence (CCC) from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association Experience with the pediatric populations Experience providing services in Spanish Experience providing services to a variety of demographic populations Preferred Qualifications More than five years of clinical experience Experience with program development Experience with a specialty area such as AAC, feeding, aural (re)habilitation, literacy, velopharyngeal incompetence, or motor speech disorders Experience with children birth to age 18 Experience with supervision Advanced spoken/written Spanish language skills Experience leading collaborative teams Rank To be Determined Tenure Information Career-Track (CT) FLSA Exempt Full Time/Part Time Full Time Number of Hours Worked per Week 40 Job FTE 1.0 Work Calendar Fiscal Job Category Faculty Benefits Eligible Yes - Full Benefits Rate of Pay $75,000 - $120,000 (depending on rank) Compensation Type salary at 1.0 full-time equivalency (FTE) Type of criminal background check required: Name-based criminal background check (non-security sensitive) Number of Vacancies 1 Target Hire Date 7/1/2027 Expected End Date Contact Information for Candidates Robin Samlan, PhD, MBA, CCC-SLP Associate Professor, Associate Department Head & Director of Clinical Education rsamlan@arizona.edu Open Date 9/24/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Documents Needed to Apply Curriculum Vitae (CV), Cover Letter, and One Additional Document Special Instructions to Applicant Please provide a Cover Letter that includes a description of your experience with and approach to clinical instruction, your Curriculum Vitae, and Contact information for three professional references. Notice of Availability of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report In compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act), each year the University of Arizona releases an Annual Security Report (ASR) for each of the University’s campuses. These reports disclose information including Clery crime statistics for the previous three calendar years and policies, procedures, and programs the University uses to keep students and employees safe, including how to report crimes or other emergencies and resources for crime victims. As a campus with residential housing facilities, the Main Campus ASR also includes a combined Annual Fire Safety report with information on fire statistics and fire safety systems, policies, and procedures. Paper copies of the Reports can be obtained by contacting the University Compliance Office at cleryact@arizona.edu. Apply Now Share Save Job © 2024 The Arizona Board of Regents on behalf of The University of Arizona Equal Opportunity Employer Vets/Disabled"
